{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna","id":813107,"title":"Continental Celts and the Fianna","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-20T19:48:56-08:00","id":813107,"title":"Continental Celts and the Fianna","content":"Canon depiction tends to limit the Fianna to the current areas where the Celtic peoples are (the British Isles and Brittany) plus the lands of the Celtic Diaspora in the Americas and Australia. However, I haven't seen much that discusses the areas in continental Europe where the Celtic peoples historically occupied (the rest of Gaul, parts of Spain, northern Italy, southern Germany, Bohemia, and parts of the Balkans).<br /> <br /> I always thought that odd. While there is not a strict, absolute tie between ethnic groups and the tribes, there are some strong connections historically. In 500 BC, the Fianna would have occupied a lot of Europe.<br /> <br /> Granted, those areas will have lots of other tribes there now, but shouldn't there still be a noticeable amount of Fianna as well as the others? I know it doesn't scream &quot;Celtic&quot; like the designers wanted, but there should be some French Fianna, some German, Czech, Italian, Spanish, and Balkan Fianna. Maybe only one in ten Garou, or less than a quarter or third depending on the area, but there should be some surviving Children of Stag in the rest of Europe (perhaps even Turkey!).<br /> <br /> Even if the Get of Fenris, Shadow Lords, and others invaded and killed them, some Fianna septs had to survive. Or do you think they would have disappeared in the two thousand years since the Celts reached their maximum area in 275 BC? Even if you think they'd be gone east of the Rhine and Alps, they should be a prominent population in France and Spain even now.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Interested in a poll here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T22:59:38-08:00","id":813200,"title":"","content":"I feel that this would help make Fianna the European tribe, whereas almost all of the other tribes don't and haven't isolated themselves so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T00:58:05-08:00","id":813231,"title":"","content":"Your thoughts are what I have been feeling for ages. I think it's a relic of the original American-centrisim of the line with them thinking more about the Irish in America then about actual Celts. They introduced Celtic roots to make it more original, but I don't think they read up on it properly. Considering the fact that Garou culture is more conservative and prone to keeping up their origins long into the future, this feels like a poor match.<br /> <br /> In my WoD there are large Fianna groups in France, Spain and Benelux. Smaller groups exist in mixed Caerns all over Europe, but they have been slowly dying out thanks to low Garou natality and the fact that they might die before they properly mange to educate their children in their culture. There may be old Caerns, Fetishes, shrines, legends and other relics of the old Fianna accross Europe but the further you get from West Europe, the less there will be actual Fianna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T09:54:57-08:00","id":813449,"title":"","content":"Bah, stereotype problem I guess.<br /> I set a lot of chronicles in northern italy. Full of fianna in the west part with fenris; fenris, fangs and shadow lords in the eastern part. Red talons alla across the alps in small numbers.<br /> I prefer to look at history and ethno-history instead of wta books sometimes (to set a chronicle, obviously).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T13:57:35-08:00","id":813623,"title":"","content":"The only time White Wolf really acknowledged this is through the camp &quot;Whispering Rovers&quot; who are intended to be descended from the mainland Celts but have more of a Strider personality to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T18:21:58-08:00","id":813793,"title":"","content":"Good to hear I am not the only one to think like this. I know there have been sporadic mentions of the Fianna in non-Celtic lands (nowadays), but as far as I know other than lip service, there's been no real information or support.<br /> <br /> I'll likely be introducing some Fianna in these non-Celtic countries soon in my chronicle, and keep the essentials of the Tribe of Stag, but show the homids in a decidedly non-Celtic culture. So I was looking for a reality check here.<br /> <br /> My thoughts are very close to Asmodai's. Fianna very prevalent in France and Spain, but ever declining populations the farther east you go. I like the idea there are some Bavarian, Czech, and Serbian Fianna packs and even septs even if they are just a handful. It's a good way to introduce some variety in the Tribe that isn't forced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T23:51:32-08:00","id":813950,"title":"","content":"Actually the first TB Fianna mentioned, that the Fianna followed the Fae from the cradle of mankind to Tir Na Nog (Ireland), but that not all made it and there remained celts in Europe everywhere, but these weren't Fianna yet, but some kind of proto-Fianna. I guess these could have become members of other tribes, or still be garou who think of themselves as Fianna.<br /> <br /> Coming from the same roots doesn't make one the same people. And it could very well be, that over the millenia any garou born to these celtic groups in europe went extinct or were assimilated. Balkans are awfully close to Shadow Lord and to some extend Black Furie territories. Italy would be Glass Walkers or House &quot;Whatever&quot; (the extinct Silver Fang house).<br /> <br /> In the canon of our LARP game we had a huge proto-Fianna sept in south Germany, but it was destroyed in the 18th century, with their caern being literally sucked up by a wyrm spirit. What remained are some scattered Fianna, who have to look to Ireland and the UK to be reminded of their cultural heritage, for what they had in Germany 200-something years ago is all gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, the stereotyping of the tribes and linkage to clich\u00e9s of human culture was a design flaw, compared to Forsaken. But, it also is part of the game we love, and I find it unfavourably to retcon it to much for political correctness or special snowflakes - like Wendigo in Africa or Uktena in Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T00:50:52-08:00","id":813966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=813950#post813950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Coming from the same roots doesn't make one the same people. And it could very well be, that over the millenia any garou born to these celtic groups in europe went extinct or were assimilated. Balkans are awfully close to Shadow Lord and to some extend Black Furie territories. Italy would be Glass Walkers or House &quot;Whatever&quot; (the extinct Silver Fang house).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words about Italy as an example for my chronicle:<br /> <br /> My main chronicle is set in the north-eastern territory of Italy.<br /> Personally, we are full of celtic, germanic, venetian and also slavic nomencaltures as names for streets, surnames, mountains ecc.<br /> I did a personal research and I can assure you all, this a melting pot of central and southern european cultures, you can also see it in our regional food, on our architecture and also in our faces.<br /> When I builded up my chronicle background, I put a lot of Fianna, a Get in Piemonte and Lombardy, but also glass walkers, bone gnawers and some black furies (ancient caern, always strugglin' with the fenris who comes with ostrogoths and Langobards).<br /> About Veneto, Trentino and Friuli: I did a research about history and ethno history, the first people who comes here was the ancient veneti, descend from an Illirian and Slavic tribes mixed. Symbols and folklore was very near to the ancient slavs.<br /> After that, the roman conquered the land and all the Cisalpine Gaul become a mix of celtic, roman and ancient venetian people.<br /> During the roman empire a lot of germanic people was deported from germany to lombardy/veneto: the romans was impressed by their agricolture and the Po valley is perfect as an enormous agricultural field.<br /> After that, Attila destroied everything and we suffered a demographic negative escalation. Then, the Ostrogoths conquered Italy. A lot of cities report this here: Rovigo from ''Hrotheigs'', Codega from ''Gothic'', and a lot of words from the venetian lenguage resemble this like ''Goto'' - glass '' or surnames.<br /> After the gothic wars, comes the Longobards.<br /> As we were the lombard ''Austria'', I can stay here for ours writing about longobards culture and heritage. Even when they were conquered by the Franks, they never disappeared. Even during the 1200 a.c. northern Italy was called ''Langbardland'' by germans and french.<br /> Also, in Northern Veneto we have a large ''cimbrian'' comunity, from bavaria.<br /> After that, Venice started growing and we were venetians for more than a thousand years. Venice was more concerned in trades and relationship with the eastern part of europe: serbian, croatian and hungarians joined venice as mercenary to fight the eternal enemies: the turks. You can find a discrete number of slavic and hungians surname in veneto and friuli.<br /> Napoleon destroied our country and then we became austrian, and finally Italy bought the Tri-Veneto and we became italians.<br /> <br /> Now, after this little historycal excursus:<br /> <br /> Probably Fianna and mayve Silver fangs comes up for first. After that, Black Furies and Warders of Man comes with the romans. Of course, the fenris comes with the germanic people, with the Longobards they were probably dominant e very powerful.<br /> With venice, I like to think about some Shadow Lords allied with the Fenris to fight the turks, also with some Silver Fangs from the venetian Nobility.<br /> Warders of Man and bone gnawers fights against the vampires in venice and other cities.<br /> So, basically, the modern northern italy garou population could be made up of Fenris, Glass Walkers &gt; Fianna, Shadow Lords, Bone Gnawers &gt; Black Furies, Silver Fangs.<br /> Even in rage across the world a fenrir talk about northern italy.<br /> About the red talons: the venetian government is working for real about the re-introduction fo the wolves pupulation near Verona and Vicenza. Actually we have a few packs made up of italian and euroasiatic wolves from eastern europe. This could be a great occasion for the Margrave: help the red talons to retake the alps and make stronger alliance with the Fenris and other tribes.<br /> The main inner-caern focus during our chronicle is the rivality between the fenris and the furies, the attempt of the shadow lords to put their claws on the italian crimes and with the fenris as brute force, the bone gnawers and the glass walkers as vampire-hunters and mediators between the fenris and the furies.<br /> <br /> Actually, this is what I often do to build my chronicle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Hope can be inspirational for someone.<br /> Sorry for my rusty english.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T02:31:10-08:00","id":814005,"title":"","content":"There are canonical examples of Fianna septs in Europe in the modern day. Fianna revised specifies that there are several in the Basque Country and Spain generally, and in World of Rage, the Fianna were very strong in rural France. I don't have any specific examples at hand, but yes, there are strong Fianna remnants in other Celtic areas, though they don't really have any sway in the Balkans (that's SL/BF turf, more or less, with some CoG influence) and are mostly in Western Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T02:49:29-08:00","id":814012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=813950#post813950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or Uktena in Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what are the Ainu then? They are pretty much the kind of group that the Uktena have been mixing with globally in the past 500 years. I could even see there being some Uktena in siberia, korea and china, who went the same way the Wendigo did.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit iffuer on how to put Wendigo in Africa. But I'm sure we could find a cannibal spirit who could be an avatar of wendigo and who needed guardians/agents and thusly tasked a group of Wendigo to travel somewhere and start a strange sept that would create a subgroup of Wendigo as different as the Siberakh.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T07:54:05-08:00","id":814126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=814012#post814012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what are the Ainu then? They are pretty much the kind of group that the Uktena have been mixing with globally in the past 500 years. I could even see there being some Uktena in siberia, korea and china, who went the same way the Wendigo did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the presence of Uktena and Wendigo in Russia, as detailed in RAR, and the fact that the Ainu were also present in Russia in larger numbers prior to the Russo-Japanese War and WW2, those two tribes should probably have had regular contact with the Ainu, both on and off the mainland, for many, many millennia prior to the much more modern dispersal of the Uktena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T08:13:21-08:00","id":814137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=813950#post813950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, the stereotyping of the tribes and linkage to clich\u00e9s of human culture was a design flaw, compared to Forsaken. But, it also is part of the game we love, and I find it unfavourably to retcon it to much for political correctness or special snowflakes - like Wendigo in Africa or Uktena in Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, that those stereotypes do not reflect the actual countries and their stereotypes at all. It is not overtly politically to correct to make sure the sources of the tribes are based on actual fact, rather than stereotypes made by another country entirely. There have been people here from Brazil complaining how off the mark the books portrayed their country. I prefer the writers to consider that others than just Americans play the games, and do research.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:04:29-08:00","id":814275,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea. Maybe garou culture being the secluded brutal secretive band of cult like indoctrination and heavy handed dealings with heirarchy and the traditions of storytelling and oral history keeping is in line with what their core tribal beluefs are. They are not human and due to their Rage and ties to garou belief and the myriad spiritual ties held to fanatically and the mental strain of dealing with ever growing rise of an enemy that the rest of the world has no idea or concept of but to them is very real and dangerous thing that they are only reflections of things we as humans may identify with. They are not apart of human society. The things they hear about are second, third hand at best and maybe their stereitypes come from that need to hold onto something they can identify a closeness too with others in the same dilema to stop their minds from slipping away entirely.<br /> <br /> They are not apart of a human culture or society. They are a seperated group that happened upon certain areas during the migration and split of the first tribe and now hold tightly to anything that still resembles the core elements of the original beliefs their tribe once held too rather than let it slip away from them.<br /> <br /> An alienation from the world and its people made even more obvious by how easily we all look at them and know they would not fit in. They do not resemble what we know or believe. There is no place for them among us.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:35:30-08:00","id":814313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=814275#post814275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea. Maybe garou culture being the secluded brutal secretive band of cult like indoctrination and heavy handed dealings with heirarchy and the traditions of storytelling and oral history keeping is in line with what their core tribal beluefs are. They are not human and due to their Rage and ties to garou belief and the myriad spiritual ties held to fanatically and the mental strain of dealing with ever growing rise of an enemy that the rest of the world has no idea or concept of but to them is very real and dangerous thing that they are only reflections of things we as humans may identify with. They are not apart of human society. The things they hear about are second, third hand at best and maybe their stereitypes come from that need to hold onto something they can identify a closeness too with others in the same dilema to stop their minds from slipping away entirely.<br /> <br /> They are not apart of a human culture or society. They are a seperated group that happened upon certain areas during the migration and split of the first tribe and now hold tightly to anything that still resembles the core elements of the original beliefs their tribe once held too rather than let it slip away from them.<br /> <br /> An alienation from the world and its people made even more obvious by how easily we all look at them and know they would not fit in. They do not resemble what we know or believe. There is no place for them among us.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, that I personally find the explanation why garou act like stereotypes being that they are not human, a little dismissive of the issues raised.<br /> <br /> Because the problem is not that garou are inhuman and monsters who hold their own laws and traditions. That is well understood. That does not, however, take from the fact that a lot of the tribal concepts are real stereotypes made by people from one country. Which are often ignorant or just outright false.<br /> <br /> Besides, garou are a fictional concept written by bunch of people in our world. Why they were stereotyped as such is due to the writers wanting to use the concepts in their game, without doing the proper research. Which the writers have now spent a good time fixing because what was written WAS pretty bad.<br /> <br /> And in-universe, most garou today are homids. Who most likely grew up ignorant of their true nature until their change (books are pretty varied on that, granted). Regardless of garou training, they would still hold some remnants of their human cultures.<br /> <br /> Again, the problem isn't that there is a drunk Fianna or a Nazi Fenrir. Rather, its that poor research caused writers to limit a tribe and its spread due to poor research.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:39:38-08:00","id":814389,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but we're aware of that problem. We are aware of the stereotypes and how they dont represent actual peoples from actual places. It's a terrible and awful failing. But we are all aware of it. This isnt to dismiss, it's a possible alternate view to use icly in the realm where we cant roll our eyes or keep posting the same scathing sentiments towards the writers until the fix is done or we come up with our own alternative in game with our players. I just offered one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:47:06-08:00","id":814394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=814389#post814389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but we're aware of that problem. We are aware of the stereotypes and how they dont represent actual peoples from actual places. It's a terrible and awful failing. But we are all aware of it. This isnt to dismiss, it's a possible alternate view to use icly in the realm where we cant roll our eyes or keep posting the same scathing sentiments towards the writers until the fix is done or we come up with our own alternative in game with our players. I just offered one.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they have fixed a lot, all ready. The 20th editions and, despite its flaws, the BNS have done a lot to fix things up in WtA. There is no reason to try to explain the old stereotypes, when they all ready have been handled. In this thread, we all ready mostly agreed that Fianna could be found where the celts were, as well.<br /> <br /> And, if I sound like I'm dismissing the writers, I'm sorry. I'm not blaming them on the stuff in 1st editions. The discussion of reality VS stereotypes just tends to come up a lot in WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:52:23-08:00","id":814399,"title":"","content":"Mostly because the same people keep bringing it up, on any thread in any forum they can and likely will continue to do after the fixes are in.<br /> <br /> Glad to see everyone here came up with answer fir the question though. That's always a positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:54:08-08:00","id":814401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=814399#post814399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly because the same people keep bringing it up, on any thread in any forum they can and likely will continue to do after the fixes are in.<br /> <br /> Glad to see everyone here came up with answer fir the question though. That's always a positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is sadly the reality of this game series. Or RPGs in general.<br /> <br /> But yes, I like that people mostly offered ideas and answers ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T17:47:21-08:00","id":814557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=813950#post813950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, the stereotyping of the tribes and linkage to clich\u00e9s of human culture was a design flaw, compared to Forsaken. But, it also is part of the game we love, and I find it unfavourably to retcon it to much for political correctness or special snowflakes - like Wendigo in Africa or Uktena in Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it's not an issue of making changes willy nilly. It's what actually makes sense for a Tribe based on a better knowledge of history and culture rather than the (seemingly) more limited knowledge (or interest) that was the basis of the original depiction in the tribebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T19:47:34-08:00","id":814616,"title":"","content":"I have a question not that I dislike the Fianna getting more of a broadening but why would they intrinsically have a monopoly on the Celts? Why not the White Howlers? Or the Fenrir who's Totem becomes demonized by the in coming Germanic peoples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T22:51:03-08:00","id":814680,"title":"","content":"They wouldn't have a monopoly on the Celts for the same reason. It's just that originally, the Celts were likely strongly Fianna, but it doesn't have to be exclusively so. Some of the Celts in the lands that are now Germanic might have been Get of Fenris for example. Or that there was an overlap between White Howlers and the Celts at the same time as the Fianna.<br /> <br /> In my personal canon for my Chronicles, I see the White Howlers being a very ancient Tribe whose human kinfolk were the original inhabitants of Europe (Old Europe - the Europe of the Neolithic and older) before the Indo-European languages arrived. That's because some people think the Picts were one of the last of the original inhabitants of Europe. It is believed the Basques are also one of the surviving groups of such people. So originally I think the White Howlers occupied much of Ice Age Europe, and only some time later did the Fianna, Get, etc. arrive.<br /> <br /> I don't mind some Tribes being strongly linked to certain cultures or ethnic groups. It is just not exclusively so (though I think the higher Pure Breeds will be strongly associated with those).<br /> <br /> The Celts (and any other ancient cultures) as a group did not exist at the time of the Tribes first formed. However, I believe if you are going to go with the idea that certain cultures are strongly associated with certain Tribes, then that logic should not be limited to where those cultures/languages exist now, but also to where they existed in the past. Since the game says there are ties to the Celtic peoples now, then it is natural to say that was true way in the past when the locations of those peoples were very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T18:10:42-08:00","id":815154,"title":"","content":"Well what &quot;Celts&quot; are is a vexed question. Technically only the Hallstatt people are Celts as they spoke Proto-Celtic, which it is thought to have spread via trade to France\\Gaul, Spain, Britain and Ireland. The Gauls for example would have been Celticised. So the Fianna could have been in Western Europe before and got Celticised as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:23:12-08:00","id":825422,"title":"","content":"As a Fianna spanish player i agree wholeheartedly with this thread. Speaking very generally and loosely about Spanish history, the pre-roman invasion spanish tribes were classified in three broad groups: Celts, Celtiberian and Iberian (based mainly in its culture and the grade of external forces -read it as Greek / Phoenician / Carthaginian forces- influence in them). <br /> <br /> The south-east Peninsular areas, closer or in direct contact with the Mediterranean Sea (that is to say, Murcia, Comunidad Valenciana, Catalu\u00f1a) were the Iberians; the most influenced by foreigners. This influence would greatly diminish the further you'd travel into the Peninsula, with the Celtiberian tribes holding (more or less) the south of actual Aragon,Madrid and roughly the north of Castilla la Mancha. The Celts would hold roughly a third/quarter of all the Iberian Peninsula, more or less the Northwest. There were some tribes, like the Vettones (Mainly in Salamanca, and the north of Caceres) or the Lusitanians (fierce warriors from Portugal) who are considered proto-celtics nowadays. <br /> <br /> The Spanish areas in which you can really feel the celtic roots are mainly Galicia and Asturias (well, also Le\u00f3n,as the Astures were as much above the Cantabrian Range as in that southern area from them; el Bierzo is one of those places of Le\u00f3n in which you cannot deny the celtic influence), but also Cantabria and Pa\u00eds Vasco. <br /> <br /> In our game group, is general consensus about Galicia, Asturias and Le\u00f3n being Fianna protectorates. Silent Striders are fairly common in the Peninsula, of course, since they were there way before the Muslim invasion of the Peninsula, and after it their numbers just increased. There are also Black Furies (mainly along the Iberian areas) protectorates, and Blood Talons clinging to the forestal areas in the center and north of Spain. Madrid; Barcelona and some other big cities have their fare share of Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers. Children of Gaia are common in Salamanca and Caceres, trying to make amends with the Bull spirist and Apis ghosts remaining in the area (in Salamanca are common the &quot;Verracos&quot; - big stone sculpures depicting bulls-). [Well, in fact the Apis are not completely extinct in our game]. Silver Fangs tend to cling to Madrid and Barcelona areas, with some surprising protectorates in Pais Vasco, Granada and Le\u00f3n (as they were really important back in the Middle Ages). Shadow Lords are rare, but usually they can be found in the same places as Silver Fangs, clinging to those same power areas. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T23:42:54-08:00","id":825803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=825422#post825422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Fianna spanish player i agree wholeheartedly with this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad it's been useful. At first glance, it seems some parts of the world are very mono-tribal except for some urban or ecumenical tribes. However, there are a lot of countries where knowledge of history (especially ancient history) reveals opportunity for involving a lot more tribes. Because players generally like more options, it gives them these options.<br /> <br /> The old sourcebooks are usually limited to the settler/immigrant nations or large continental regions that give variety of all the tribes. Chronicles set in European countries, on the surface, seem very limited - pick the ethnic tribe plus Glass Walkers, Bone Gnawers, and perhaps Silver Fangs and one other tribe. It's good when more options for players (and STs) can be added that make sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T01:05:29-08:00","id":825833,"title":"","content":"I have found that exploring history and mythology is key to a good understanding of the Werewolf context and creating a more interesting and broad setting for them to engage in. When we get around to the &quot;Lore of the Clans&quot; equivalent for Werewolf, I really hope that they will be considering this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T14:15:29-08:00","id":1190006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=825422#post825422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Fianna spanish player i agree wholeheartedly with this thread. Speaking very generally and loosely about Spanish history, the pre-roman invasion spanish tribes were classified in three broad groups: Celts, Celtiberian and Iberian (based mainly in its culture and the grade of external forces -read it as Greek / Phoenician / Carthaginian forces- influence in them).<br /> <br /> The south-east Peninsular areas, closer or in direct contact with the Mediterranean Sea (that is to say, Murcia, Comunidad Valenciana, Catalu\u00f1a) were the Iberians; the most influenced by foreigners. This influence would greatly diminish the further you'd travel into the Peninsula, with the Celtiberian tribes holding (more or less) the south of actual Aragon,Madrid and roughly the north of Castilla la Mancha. The Celts would hold roughly a third/quarter of all the Iberian Peninsula, more or less the Northwest. There were some tribes, like the Vettones (Mainly in Salamanca, and the north of Caceres) or the Lusitanians (fierce warriors from Portugal) who are considered proto-celtics nowadays.<br /> <br /> The Spanish areas in which you can really feel the celtic roots are mainly Galicia and Asturias (well, also Le\u00f3n,as the Astures were as much above the Cantabrian Range as in that southern area from them; el Bierzo is one of those places of Le\u00f3n in which you cannot deny the celtic influence), but also Cantabria and Pa\u00eds Vasco.<br /> <br /> In our game group, is general consensus about Galicia, Asturias and Le\u00f3n being Fianna protectorates. Silent Striders are fairly common in the Peninsula, of course, since they were there way before the Muslim invasion of the Peninsula, and after it their numbers just increased. There are also Black Furies (mainly along the Iberian areas) protectorates, and Blood Talons clinging to the forestal areas in the center and north of Spain. Madrid; Barcelona and some other big cities have their fare share of Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers. Children of Gaia are common in Salamanca and Caceres, trying to make amends with the Bull spirist and Apis ghosts remaining in the area (in Salamanca are common the &quot;Verracos&quot; - big stone sculpures depicting bulls-). [Well, in fact the Apis are not completely extinct in our game]. Silver Fangs tend to cling to Madrid and Barcelona areas, with some surprising protectorates in Pais Vasco, Granada and Le\u00f3n (as they were really important back in the Middle Ages). Shadow Lords are rare, but usually they can be found in the same places as Silver Fangs, clinging to those same power areas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is awesome! I am a Brazilian ST, and I am just starting a new chronicle in Spain (my first one actually) and only recently I became aware of this forum. We picked Spain because of the rich culture, amazing history and beautiful landscape, as well as the lack of a stereotypically prevailing Tribe, which would ease the new players (who want to create characters of various tribes) into the setting and WtA in general. My general idea is to create a chronicle around a powerful, multi Tribe caern, with significant internal struggles, which are fueled by various outside agents that are actually using this caern as a proxy war of sorts to the European power grab race. On my story, with the decline of the Silver Fangs in Europe (their last bastions being in France and Spain), the Glass Walkers (coming from various European capitals) the Get of Fenris (from the north and northwest) and the Shadow Lords (from the east) are all attempting to fill the power gap, forging alliances with the other tribes. This is, of course, the background for the microverse where the players will be inserted, which is the sept.<br /> However, since this is my first story, I am having trouble measuring power levels and numbers for the Garou (the Fianna especially, and the extent to which their native peoples had a presence in Andaluc\u00eda), as well as coming up with actual wyrm things to oppose the Garou in the region. Part of this is actually lack of knowledge of local myths, as well as local current geopolitics.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if you (or anyone really) have any tips on figuring out specific numbers and power level for the Garou and the sept based on the various Tribes that have a significant presence in Spain (maybe based on your own games). The idea is for the sept to be located at the Sierra Nevada (protecting at caern of at least Level 3), with the players starting in Granada before the First Change (I figured it would be a great opportunity to teach them the WtA setting and what it means to be Garou in game).<br /> <br /> I figured the sept would be ruled by a small (and decaying) group of Silver Fangs (maybe Blood Red Crest or Gleaming Eye), which are clinging to power at the expense of the sept. At the caern proper there would be significant Fianna (maybe local or from Pa\u00eds Vasco), Get of Fenris (descendants from Northern Italy Get, now local) and Black Furies (local) presence, a Shadow Lord emissary, as well as travelling Silent Striders. The Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers would have a minor caern (Level 1 probably) nearby (maybe in Granada, the Generalife Park looks like a good location).<br /> <br /> What do you guys, think?<br /> <br /> (P.S.: I know the post is old, but it is very on point, so why not give it a try)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23922-kinguir","name":"Kinguir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T20:02:47-08:00","id":1190112,"title":"","content":"Canonically the tribes most frequently mentioned with Spain are Children of Gaia, the Glass Walkers, the Silent Striders, and the Shadow Lords (for some strange reason I don't understand). Silver Fangs have been there too.<br /> <br /> If you go by history and match ethnic groups with Garou tribes, you get a different mix. You likely start with Fianna (from the Celtiberians) and Silent Striders. Maybe even small numbers of Red Talons. Glass Walkers would arrive when the Romans came. Spain was a very developed part of the Empire by the time it fell. The Goths and Vandals who arrived during the barbarian invasions probably had some Get of Fenris with them. The general population of tribes probably settled there with some additional influx from Berbers arriving after the Muslim conquest. So sprinkle in some Children of Gaia, Black Furies, and Bone Gnawers as needed. Plus one SF house.<br /> <br /> The exact mix today is up to whatever you need it to be for your chronicle. As my base of the most populous tribes, I'd start with Fianna. Then the Get and Glass Walkers. Then the others as you'd like. Increase or decrease their relative numbers as you'd like. If you want to add an odd tribe that doesn't seem it should be there, come up with some excuse in Garou history to explain them holding one or more caerns.<br /> <br /> Your ideas seem plausible and wouldn't cause me to raise an eyebrow. I think you can trust your judgment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T09:36:01-08:00","id":1190306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=1190112#post1190112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically the tribes most frequently mentioned with Spain are Children of Gaia, the Glass Walkers, the Silent Striders, and the Shadow Lords (for some strange reason I don't understand). Silver Fangs have been there too.<br /> <br /> If you go by history and match ethnic groups with Garou tribes, you get a different mix. You likely start with Fianna (from the Celtiberians) and Silent Striders. Maybe even small numbers of Red Talons. Glass Walkers would arrive when the Romans came. Spain was a very developed part of the Empire by the time it fell. The Goths and Vandals who arrived during the barbarian invasions probably had some Get of Fenris with them. The general population of tribes probably settled there with some additional influx from Berbers arriving after the Muslim conquest. So sprinkle in some Children of Gaia, Black Furies, and Bone Gnawers as needed. Plus one SF house.<br /> <br /> The exact mix today is up to whatever you need it to be for your chronicle. As my base of the most populous tribes, I'd start with Fianna. Then the Get and Glass Walkers. Then the others as you'd like. Increase or decrease their relative numbers as you'd like. If you want to add an odd tribe that doesn't seem it should be there, come up with some excuse in Garou history to explain them holding one or more caerns.<br /> <br /> Your ideas seem plausible and wouldn't cause me to raise an eyebrow. I think you can trust your judgment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reply! I was indeed going largely by history and ethnic groups, which seems to be consistent with what you said.<br /> <br /> The general idea was to make a sept where there would be no prevalent power base for any Tribe, which is one of the reasons the SFs managed to stay in power. From a Garou politics perspective (I don't know if this is canon or not, but it is the impression I have) SFs have been reduced to a number of low level caerns througout Europe, losing a lot of ground to the other Tribes since the middle ages. The only powerful caerns that they would still rule would be multi tribe caerns, where the Tribes' power bases clash somewhat and there is no one dominant Tribe, which seems to be where the continental Fianna are stronger (France and Spain, mainly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23922-kinguir","name":"Kinguir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T12:49:51-08:00","id":1190393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kinguir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=1190306#post1190306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the reply! I was indeed going largely by history and ethnic groups, which seems to be consistent with what you said.<br /> <br /> The general idea was to make a sept where there would be no prevalent power base for any Tribe, which is one of the reasons the SFs managed to stay in power. From a Garou politics perspective (I don't know if this is canon or not, but it is the impression I have) SFs have been reduced to a number of low level caerns througout Europe, losing a lot of ground to the other Tribes since the middle ages. The only powerful caerns that they would still rule would be multi tribe caerns, where the Tribes' power bases clash somewhat and there is no one dominant Tribe, which seems to be where the continental Fianna are stronger (France and Spain, mainly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also I wanted to add that Galacia has maintained more of a Celtic Iberian Claire compared to the rest of Spain. The Fianna revised tribe book does bring this up if I remember. Also Spain and Ireland have had a long history of sailors passing through/washing up/remaining on one another's shores (especially Galacia). Heck the old Sea shanty that Capt. Quint from Jaws kept singing (&quot;Sweet Spanish Ladies&quot;) was about Irish sailors in the British Navey who started families in Spain and then were call out of port. There are tons of reasons for a Spanish Fianna presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T14:25:57-08:00","id":1190440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=1190112#post1190112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically the tribes most frequently mentioned with Spain are Children of Gaia, the Glass Walkers, the Silent Striders, and the Shadow Lords (for some strange reason I don't understand). Silver Fangs have been there too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the Shadow Lords are easy enough to explain- they were slated to be the 'bad guys' that invaded the Americas alongside the conquistadors, missionaries, and other agents of Imperial Spain. Ergo, they have to have a presence in the old country prior to the invasion. I think that is as deep as the logic goes, sadly. <br /> <br /> I don't think it makes much thematic sense (at least not without workshoping it a lot), but there you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T17:57:30-08:00","id":1190495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813107-continental-celts-and-the-fianna?p=1190440#post1190440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, the Shadow Lords are easy enough to explain- they were slated to be the 'bad guys' that invaded the Americas alongside the conquistadors, missionaries, and other agents of Imperial Spain. Ergo, they have to have a presence in the old country prior to the invasion. I think that is as deep as the logic goes, sadly.<br /> <br /> I don't think it makes much thematic sense (at least not without workshoping it a lot), but there you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>A possible explanation might be that the Visigoths picked up some Shadow Lord kinfolk while they controlled what is now Ukraine, and after they Huns kicked them out and they entered the Roman Empire (and eventually Spain), that there was enough Shadow Lord kinfolk and accompanying Shadow Lords that they were able to control one or other small number of caerns in Spain. It would have to be a small number compared to other tribes though.<br /> <br /> Or simply say a small number of Shadow Lords invaded one or more caerns by moonbridge and took them over, but of course they'd be without kinfolk and would have to create everything as they went. But it would be the kind of thing an individual Shadow Lord (and his pack or other followers) might do for a Challenge, as create a colony where none might be. But that kind of thing would have to be rare.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:55:43-08:00","id":1190670,"title":"","content":"I just ignore the Spanish Shadow Lords. Like The Laughing Stranger said, I think it was another example of making them into the &quot;bad guy&quot; tribe by linking them with the Conquistadors. <br /> <br /> I used the Fianna for that instead. It lead to the creation of a Mexican camp that revers the local deer and hunting incarna, Camaxtli.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 03-01-2018, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T08:27:30-08:00","id":1190674,"title":"","content":"Never mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 03-01-2018, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}